From ab0b553cf3e2e16d39e5c1e1f1f5451bba774995 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Henrique <samueloph@debian.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:07:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sws: fix connection-monitor for connections closed before a
 request

sws updates its connection-monitor state only when it parses a request.
Since 5232c1620897 it no longer clears the state after the first logged
disconnect, so the state a test sets with connection-monitor remains
after that test ends. If the next test that uses the same server closes
a connection before sws has parsed any request of that test, sws logs
[DISCONNECT] even if that test does not use connection-monitor.

Tests 3231 and 3232 do that: they close a CONNECT_ONLY connection, which
never sent anything, before the HTTP transfer sends its request. They
fail with an unexpected [DISCONNECT] in server.input whenever the state
is still enabled from a previous test, such as 3223 to 3226. With
parallel test runners this depends on which runner picks up the test,
so the failures look random. Most Debian package builds of 8.23.0-rc1
failed like this. To reproduce, run this in the tests directory:

  ./runtests.pl 3226 3231

When a connection closes while the test number is unset
(DOCNUMBER_NOTHING), read it from server.cmd, as sws already does for
requests without one. Then use the connection-monitor setting of that
test, or disable connection monitoring if there is no test number. A
test using connection-monitor now gets [DISCONNECT] logged for a
connection closed before its first request, regardless of the previous
test.

Ref: #22902
Follow-up to 5232c1620897213db1781937c0bace0b7320474f #22159
---
 tests/server/sws.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/server/sws.c b/tests/server/sws.c
index 5587e50feaf7..e41d3d5eb993 100644
--- a/tests/server/sws.c
+++ b/tests/server/sws.c
@@ -2131,6 +2131,17 @@ static int test_sws(int argc, const char *argv[])
             goto sws_cleanup;

           if(rc < 0) {
+            if(req->testno == DOCNUMBER_NOTHING) {
+              /* The test number is unknown here, so connmon may be left over
+                 from a previous test case, for example when a client closes
+                 a connection without sending anything. Use the setting of
+                 the test case in server.cmd, or disable it without one. */
+              req->connmon = FALSE;
+              parse_cmdfile(req);
+              if(req->testno != DOCNUMBER_NOTHING)
+                sws_parse_servercmd(req);
+            }
+
             logmsg("====> Client disconnect %d", req->connmon);

             if(req->connmon) {
